    "en": "Nenmatsu-chōsei is the company's year-end recalculation of your income tax: tax is withheld monthly as an estimate, then settled exactly — overpayments come back in your December salary, shortfalls are deducted. Foreign company workers in Japan go through it just like Japanese staff.",
